comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-27T19:29:06.473Z","harness:codex","Evidence: pm test pm-8pnj --run --progress executed all seven linked commands successfully. Exact coverage is 59,885/59,885 statements, 45,077/45,077 branches, 12,452/12,452 functions, and 57,669/57,669 lines; packed npx, 88-command package-first dogfood, and packed bunx acceptance all exited 0."
  "2026-08-27T19:30:08.193Z","harness:codex","Investigation note: the initial linked history-drift command refused under schema context because the source tracker has 2,572 items and the sandbox schema context has zero. The link now explicitly declares pm_context_mode=tracker; no trust override or real tracker mutation was used by the test runner."
  "2026-08-27T20:37:19.855Z","harness:codex","Corrective lifecycle started after exact-head review: preserve all earlier hash-chain entries, append current verification and hosted receipts before the new close events, then release the reopened canonical items. No prior close/release evidence will be rewritten."
  "2026-08-27T21:13:32.776Z","harness:codex","Corrective lifecycle evidence 2026-08-27: the canonical items were reopened, claimed, and kept in progress while implementation and all available local verification were appended. pm test pm-8pnj then recorded seven passing linked commands before any renewed close or release, including exact coverage plus real packed npx, bunx, and package-first temporary-directory acceptance. No historical event was rewritten."
  "2026-08-27T21:32:00.011Z","harness:codex","Final lifecycle proof 2026-08-27: pm-wa39rl, pm-ok2kdn, pm-fo8g7j, and pm-k23c4c were each closed and released only after their focused, exact-coverage, package, and where applicable full hosted-matrix evidence had been appended. This corrective sequence preserves every prior hash-chained event."
  "2026-08-27T22:10:52.786Z","harness:codex","Graph evidence: base head had 1,342 prose-edge gaps; the lifecycle-proof comment added exactly four untyped pairs from pm-ervmsc to pm-wa39rl, pm-ok2kdn, pm-fo8g7j, and pm-k23c4c. Added directed verifies edges for those four evidence-backed relationships; no generic or inverse duplicate edges were added."
  "2026-08-28T10:28:42.066Z","harness:codex","Receipt integrity correction: linked the previously cited recursive pm-8pnj closeout run and the defect-evidence gate as first-class tests. Run test-local-mtct46ib-bv7nq1 passed the nested pm-8pnj suite, whose 7/7 executions cover focused transcript/output tests, token ratchet, release automation, exact coverage, packed npx, 88-command package dogfood, and packed bunx. Run test-local-mtct4htf-ydtivf passed the defect boundary, defect evidence, and recurrence policy gates with zero findings."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-27T19:29:07.001Z","harness:codex","Lifecycle evidence is append-only: gate evidence and reproducible test links should be recorded before close and release. When a review detects an older ordering defect, append follow-up receipts and govern the recurrence; never rewrite the original history."
  "2026-08-27T21:13:33.341Z","harness:codex","Closeout evidence is a lifecycle invariant, not just prose quality: every reproducible command and result available at delivery time must be linked and appended before close/release so history order itself proves the claim."
